## Field Notes and Rationale

### recognition_features
Structured array derived from the blueprint description ("heavy-duty mobile industrial craft designed to skim planetary surfaces and gather regolith for ISRU processing") and cross-referenced with the rh400-prompt-template.md aesthetic notes. Each feature describes WHAT is visible, not HOW to render it.

### visual_identity
Separate from recognition_features — captures the overall "feel" of the unit (heavy, industrial, rugged, modular, repairable) and the design philosophy that guides visual decisions. This is distinct from the literal visual elements listed in recognition_features.

### scale_class
Proposed value: `vehicle`. This is a new scale class not yet formalized by the Icon Bible (which is missing). Proposed scale system for future units: `human` / `vehicle` / `structure` / `megastructure`. Flagged for formalization in completion report.

### technology_level
Value: `2` (Mk2). Design System canonical value from Icon Bible Section 4 progression. Mk2 = "cleaner, welded, slight sheen." This is a reference to the Design System's single source of truth — not an invented value.

### manufacturing_style
Value: `heavy_industrial`. Design System canonical value from Icon Bible Section 5. Visual characteristics: "crude, oversized, simple geometry." This IS the Design System's definition for this category — it is not a literal value stored independently.

### color_profile
Uses semantic role references (`industrial_primary`, `industrial_secondary`, `hazard_warning`) per Gotcha 1. No literal hex values. The Design System resolves these roles to actual RGB values.

### shared_components
Empty array. Icon Bible file (`2026-07-19-HIGH-DESIGN-GALAXYGAME_ICON_BIBLE.md`) does not exist in the workspace, so no canonical component IDs are available for reference. Will be populated once the Icon Bible is located or reconstructed.

### prompt_template_refs
Empty object. Prompt template names/versions are managed separately by PromptBuilder and have not yet been established as named templates in any document.

### animation_profile
Value: `vehicles_status_lights`. Derived from Icon Bible Section 9 animation rules (vehicle category → status lights, 0.5-1s cycle). This is a Design System canonical mapping.

